Subject: [PATCH v5 1/2] media: sun6i-csi: bridge: Use V4L2 subdev active state
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 14:57:13 +0330
Message-Id: <20260719112714.72802-2-arash.golgol@gmail.com>
X-Mailer: git-send-email 2.34.1
In-Reply-To: <20260719112714.72802-1-arash.golgol@gmail.com>
References: <20260719112714.72802-1-arash.golgol@gmail.com>
Precedence: bulk
X-Mailing-List: linux-sunxi@lists.linux.dev
List-Id: <linux-sunxi.lists.linux.dev>
List-Subscribe: <mailto:linux-sunxi+subscribe@lists.linux.dev>
List-Unsubscribe: <mailto:linux-sunxi+unsubscribe@lists.linux.dev>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Use the V4L2 subdev active state API to store the active format.
This simplifies the driver not only by dropping the bridge mbus_format
field, but it also allows dropping the bridge lock, replaced with
the state lock.

Previously, capture accessed bridge private state directly. After
moving to framework-managed state, resolve the format through the
subdev pad API.

The sun6i-csi-bridge hardware does not perform any format conversion.
Enforce identical formats on the sink and source pads in the set_fmt()
and init_state() callbacks.

Signed-off-by: Arash Golgol <arash.golgol@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Paul Kocialkowski <paulk@sys-base.io>
Tested-by: Paul Kocialkowski <paulk@sys-base.io>
Reviewed-by: Laurent Pinchart <laurent.pinchart@ideasonboard.com>
